{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And all who heard shall lay their hands.</b> It is found in Torat Kohanim: What is different about this execution, that it involves semikhah? Rather, because at the time of the rendering of the verdict the witnesses must state explicitly, just as they heard from the mouth of the one who pronounced the blessing — therefore they lay their hands upon him, to say: This sin that you cause to be upon us — let it be upon you."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:26.548861139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}